[00:06.24]<b>Lord Worth:</b> Come in!
[00:08.66]<b>Mary:</b> Yes, sir?
[00:09.68]<b>Lord Worth:</b> No, no Mary... I don't want you!
[00:12.68]<b>Mary:</b> Who do you want, sir?
[00:14.04]<b>Lord Worth:</b> I want James... I want him immediately!
[00:16.64]<b>Mary:</b> Yes, sir... I'll go and find him.
[00:23.12]<b>Lord Worth:</b> Ah, James!
[00:24.44]<b>James:</b> Did you want to see me, sir?
[00:26.04]<b>Lord Worth:</b> Yes, I wanted to see you twenty minutes ago.
[00:28.84]<b>James:</b> Sorry, sir. I was in the garage.
[00:31.44]<b>Lord Worth:</b> I want a car this afternoon.
[00:33.16]<b>James:</b> Which car do you want, sir? The Rolls, the Mercedes, or the Ferrari?
[00:37.56]<b>Lord Worth:</b> Mmm... the Rolls, I think. Yes, the Rolls.
[00:41.48]<b>James:</b> Where do you want to go, sir?
[00:42.92]<b>Lord Worth:</b> Heathrow Airport Terminal 2.
[00:45.14]<b>James:</b> What time, sir?
[00:46.40]<b>Lord Worth:</b> We'll leave here after lunch... at two o'clock.
[00:51.92]<b>Lord Worth:</b> Ah, Charles!
[00:52.72]<b>Charles:</b> Yes, sir.
[00:53.78]<b>Lord Worth:</b> I want an early lunch today, Charles.
[00:55.76]<b>Charles:</b> Yes, sir... What time?
[00:57.50]<b>Lord Worth:</b> Twelve o'clock... Oh, and I want you to reserve a table at the Savoy... for seven o'clock.
[01:02.22]<b>Charles:</b> Yes, sir.
[01:03.18]<b>Lord Worth:</b> ...and I want Mary to prepare the guest room for Sir Thomas. I want her to make a special effort. Sir Thomas is a very important guest.
[01:10.26]<b>Charles:</b> Yes, sir... anything else, sir?
[01:13.36]<b>Lord Worth:</b> No, Charles, that's all.